    "sourceNullable": "{\"cells\":[{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"# VQCC / cand-0045 \u2014 bit-identical rebuild of our submitted `submission.zip` (Kaggle submission 57794709, public LB 22.98999)\\n\\n**What this notebook does.** It downloads every payload file of our submitted archive from four public Apache-2.0 Kaggle datasets\\n(`yoyobar/qcc-2298-submission-20261030` **version 1** for `invsqrt.kmb`, `busyaprime/33-qcc-v8-members` **version 6** for `dqi.kmb`,\\n`manwithacat/vqcc-apache-public-circuits` **version 30** for the 15 `dfthcsos/angle_k_*.kmb` loaders, and `heliosli/qcc-circuits-live`\\n**version 21** for `dfthcsos/submission.npz`), verifies all 18 files byte-for-byte against the pinned SHA-256 set, and re-packs them into\\n`submission.zip` with the same member order, timestamps, mode bits and deflate settings, so that the produced archive is\\nbyte-identical to the archive we submitted (Kaggle submission **57794709**, public score **22.98999**, status COMPLETE,\\n2026-10-30 05:57 UTC).\\n\\n**Competition:** [Google Quantum AI \u2014 Verifiable Quantum Circuit Compilation](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation)\\n(file submission; the archive holds one `invsqrt.kmb`, one `dqi.kmb`, a `dfthcsos/` directory with 15 ANGLE circuits and `submission.npz`).\\n\\n**Licence.** This notebook is released under the **Apache License 2.0**. It contains no circuit data of its own: every payload byte is\\nfetched at run time from the public datasets above, which carry their own `LICENSE`/`NOTICE`/`CREDITS`/manifest files crediting each\\nfile's author and source notebook. Credits for the files in this archive: `invsqrt.kmb` \u2014 yoyobar's 62-qubit construction\\n(notebook `yoyobar/lb-22-99-invsqrt-101-62-qubits`, Apache-2.0; its NOTICE credits Akmal Xodarev (busyaprime) and mrmeows' 63-qubit\\noriginal from which it is modified); `dqi.kmb` \u2014 hengck23's approximate decoder (iteration 014, 889 qubits) as packaged by busyaprime;\\ndfthcsos loaders \u2014 Heliosli (k0, k1, k4, k5, k8), Dmitrii Gluzdov (k2, k3, k14), Atakan Aldemir (k6, k7, k9\u2013k13), assembled as\\n`parts/assembly_best.json` (`d7f8223d0f9b`) of manwithacat's dataset; `dfthcsos/submission.npz` \u2014 Heliosli's table weights\\n(`qcc-circuits-live` release v40_gz8, its `CREDITS.md` names the lineage: Dmitrii Gluzdov, Ahmed Berat \u00d6zer, sigmaborov,\\nbaidalinadilzhan, Atakan Aldemir, SomeJoint). All Apache-2.0, all unchanged.\\n\\n**Why this notebook exists.** The competition's Milestone and Longest-Leader prizes require a public notebook that reproduces the\\nsubmitted archive. This is that notebook for our current best submission; it supersedes\\n`dmitriyab/vqcc-cand-0044-bit-identical-submission-rebuild` (submission 57791030, 22.88871), from which it differs in exactly one\\nmember: `invsqrt.kmb` (`9a8627c8\u2026`, 63 qubits \u2192 `a568bc79\u2026`, 62 qubits).\\n\\n**Measurements behind the submission** (full-shot official verifiers on ML Core, campaign seeds, not this notebook):\\n\\n| task | member | measured | ratio vs reference |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `invsqrt` | `a568bc79\u2026` (62 qubits) | 200,540,928 shots, 0 failures, worst error/tolerance 0.99932 at x=161, cost 101,002.54 (Q 62, 1,332.9 Toffoli, 41 rotations) | \u00d720.5619 |\\n| `dqi` | `7a378f47\u2026` (889 qubits) | 102,400 shots, 0 value / 0 phase errors on two seeds, cost 4.08399e11 | \u00d759.8421 |\\n| `dfthcsos` | 15 ANGLE + `c979cde3\u2026` npz | full 78,080 shots, PASS on seeds 20261028 and 20261029, cost 338,242,144.68, \u03bb_eff 48.359132, T 16,266, Q 430 | \u00d79.9207 |\\n\\ngeometric mean of the three ratios = **23.0251** on the campaign reference costs; the platform scored it **22.98999**.\\nThis notebook reproduces the *archive*, not those measurements \u2014 it runs no verifier and evaluates no circuit.\\n\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":\"# The submitted archive, pinned. Anything that deviates is reported as a failure.\\nEXPECT_ZIP_SHA256 = \\\"021ed1ddcc76eeeae274580a8baeed83a5fc8f2320eb361aa02fb4fa0303510e\\\"\\nEXPECT_ZIP_BYTES = 28503982\\n\\n# Four public Apache-2.0 datasets, all pinned by version number.\\nDS_YOYO = (\\\"yoyobar/qcc-2298-submission-20261030\\\", 1)        # invsqrt.kmb (62 qubits)\\nDS_BUSYA = (\\\"busyaprime/33-qcc-v8-members\\\", 6)              # dqi.kmb\\nDS_MWC = (\\\"manwithacat/vqcc-apache-public-circuits\\\", 30)   # dfthcsos loaders (assembly d7f8223d0f9b)\\nDS_HELIOS = (\\\"heliosli/qcc-circuits-live\\\", 21)             # dfthcsos/submission.npz (release v40_gz8)\\nCOMPRESSLEVEL = None         # zipfile default for ZIP_DEFLATED\\n\\n# The archive was written with ZipFile.write() from an extracted tree (mode 0o644); the member mtimes are the\\n# packaging instant (local time, MSK) except invsqrt.kmb, which kept the dataset file's mtime. They carry no\\n# meaning, but reproducing them is what makes the repack byte-identical.\\nMEMBER_MODE = 0o100644\\nMEMBER_MTIME = {\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_0.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_1.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_10.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_11.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_12.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_13.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_14.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_2.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_3.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_4.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_5.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_6.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_7.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_8.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_9.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 30),\\n    \\\"dqi.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 7, 52, 32),\\n    \\\"invsqrt.kmb\\\": (2026, 10, 30, 2, 50, 12),\\n}\\n\\n# member -> (dataset, remote file name, sha256)\\nEXPECT_MEMBERS = {\\n    \\\"invsqrt.kmb\\\": (DS_YOYO, \\\"submission/invsqrt.kmb\\\", \\\"a568bc79348165bad5be2349960d200300c5639ffd2142aca6d548e764a399d9\\\"),\\n    \\\"dqi.kmb\\\": (DS_BUSYA, \\\"dqi.kmb\\\", \\\"7a378f4755605e0c5fa6117f808891bf8dcf0797d047155e6d4c9e75e3c99421\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\": (DS_HELIOS, \\\"dfthcsos__submission.npz\\\", \\\"c979cde3209fe16218060be7485f6869aff1613a2ceff8505bf0d557fad7dfb0\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_0.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/0c646d2c5930/angle_k_0.kmb\\\", \\\"9c31da0c1d047e7dcac638df807d3cef96eac6f736a8838a0ae6943e9c46c74f\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_1.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/eb9b9c2e6baa/angle_k_1.kmb\\\", \\\"39b8d10098be097f75148639ee302249bdabe112a9278a48565eadb0cb86810b\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_2.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/e3ad4d93d0ae/angle_k_2.kmb\\\", \\\"2e8dfdeb69c496e9e510fe99722153663760980d45c35ad9b72e79ba799dde49\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_3.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/f5b6b4a6a41c/angle_k_3.kmb\\\", \\\"13817cf8d36ea112e62d7863edde2193aa5907dd0605612c4f0e1e54bacc173b\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_4.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/0c646d2c5930/angle_k_4.kmb\\\", \\\"8dce8f4a380998d818bf8a08e4f3daa62aaeb31a25d084aa57549f931a937f3d\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_5.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/e1df7e136f4f/angle_k_5.kmb\\\", \\\"42cf7d76ef0f0b36640a9e65005214fdd4d9a9bb82b8cef6e658dbbdd8417099\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_6.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_6.kmb\\\", \\\"7fd7bd333b1427ecf546b0c27717ed9428e255e5165c4db14e5f95f8af45c838\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_7.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_7.kmb\\\", \\\"809a775b98836ee00e8783d3f616bb8517bb3a3621978bc704d20b543a8df4ec\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_8.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/eb9b9c2e6baa/angle_k_8.kmb\\\", \\\"42d0deb376981d0470bebdd370ca2adf79685b4bf3e6909be262e2beced030ec\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_9.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_9.kmb\\\", \\\"f1c49e7cf8e4f3a9adaffe167d2bbe21497a52eca2c7d09f765fc5a125e304c3\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_10.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_10.kmb\\\", \\\"e75f6b0685d754bf76f3f4d62589bf1d07b118faeeb0ab8745833733286db2fc\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_11.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_11.kmb\\\", \\\"773e54f6f0d7c3f769db433f263d541cdcff1076fb75109740907e3249996141\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_12.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_12.kmb\\\", \\\"d86ca7ddd984059ded765b953cc936388517a7ca5789676ae90910a2be89769d\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_13.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/77bf305474c4/angle_k_13.kmb\\\", \\\"50d82cf65116f06c0fe469ebba312f72675b277263461ab88b4d15eca947c050\\\"),\\n    \\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_14.kmb\\\": (DS_MWC, \\\"circuits/chemistry/f5b6b4a6a41c/angle_k_14.kmb\\\", \\\"ae2070998e31b7e05d01183914df20b6974c1760bddf90d1adac86ea75c7bf3f\\\"),\\n}\\nprint(\\\"target archive:\\\", EXPECT_ZIP_SHA256, EXPECT_ZIP_BYTES, \\\"bytes;\\\", len(EXPECT_MEMBERS), \\\"members\\\")\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":\"import hashlib, json, os, sys, urllib.parse, urllib.request, zipfile, zlib\\n\\nWORK = \\\"/kaggle/working\\\"\\nPAYLOAD = os.path.join(WORK, \\\"payload\\\")\\nos.makedirs(PAYLOAD, exist_ok=True)\\nprint(\\\"python\\\", sys.version.split()[0], \\\"| zlib\\\", zlib.ZLIB_VERSION, zlib.ZLIB_RUNTIME_VERSION)\\n\\n\\ndef fetch(dataset, remote_name, dest, expect_sha):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Stream one dataset file into dest, hashing as it goes; verify sha256.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ref, version = dataset\\n    url = \\\"https://www.kaggle.com/api/v1/datasets/download/%s/%s?datasetVersionNumber=%d\\\" % (\\n        ref, urllib.parse.quote(remote_name, safe=\\\"\\\"), version)\\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\\n    n = 0\\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=120) as r, open(dest, \\\"wb\\\") as f:\\n        while True:\\n            b = r.read(1 << 22)\\n            if not b:\\n                break\\n            h.update(b)\\n            f.write(b)\\n            n += len(b)\\n    got = h.hexdigest()\\n    assert got == expect_sha, \\\"%s: sha %s != expected %s\\\" % (remote_name, got, expect_sha)\\n    return got, n\\n\\n\\nlocal = {}\\nfor member in sorted(EXPECT_MEMBERS):\\n    dataset, remote, sha_expect = EXPECT_MEMBERS[member]\\n    dest = os.path.join(PAYLOAD, member.replace(\\\"/\\\", \\\"__\\\"))\\n    sha, size = fetch(dataset, remote, dest, sha_expect)\\n    local[member] = dest\\n    print(\\\"ok  %-28s %12d bytes  %s  <- %s v%d\\\" % (member, size, sha[:16], dataset[0], dataset[1]))\\nprint(\\\"PAYLOAD_VERIFY PASS (%d files, byte-identical to the pinned dataset versions)\\\" % len(local))\\n\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":\"# Re-pack exactly the way the submitted archive was built:\\n#   * members in sorted() order (that is the order inside the submitted zip),\\n#   * ZIP_DEFLATED at the default level,\\n#   * ZipInfo with the pinned per-member date_time and mode 0o644, written via writestr.\\nOUT = os.path.join(WORK, \\\"submission.zip\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef sha_file(p):\\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\\n    with open(p, \\\"rb\\\") as f:\\n        for b in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 24), b\\\"\\\"):\\n            h.update(b)\\n    return h.hexdigest()\\n\\n\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(OUT, \\\"w\\\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED, compresslevel=COMPRESSLEVEL) as z:\\n    for member in sorted(local):\\n        info = zipfile.ZipInfo(\\n            filename=member,\\n            date_time=MEMBER_MTIME[member],\\n        )\\n        info.compress_type = zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED   # a hand-built ZipInfo defaults to STORED\\n        info.external_attr = MEMBER_MODE << 16      # ZipFile.write() stored the file mode; writestr would not\\n        with open(local[member], \\\"rb\\\") as f:\\n            z.writestr(info, f.read())\\n\\nzip_sha = sha_file(OUT)\\nzip_bytes = os.path.getsize(OUT)\\nprint(\\\"rebuilt :\\\", zip_sha, zip_bytes, \\\"bytes\\\")\\nprint(\\\"target  :\\\", EXPECT_ZIP_SHA256, EXPECT_ZIP_BYTES, \\\"bytes\\\")\\n\\nMEMBERS_MATCH = True\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(OUT) as z:\\n    names = z.namelist()\\n    assert names == sorted(EXPECT_MEMBERS), names\\n    for member in names:\\n        got = hashlib.sha256(z.read(member)).hexdigest()\\n        if got != EXPECT_MEMBERS[member][2]:\\n            MEMBERS_MATCH = False\\n            print(\\\"MEMBER MISMATCH\\\", member, got)\\n\\nBIT_IDENTICAL = (zip_sha == EXPECT_ZIP_SHA256 and zip_bytes == EXPECT_ZIP_BYTES)\\nprint()\\nprint(\\\"members_identical (hard check) :\\\", MEMBERS_MATCH)\\nprint(\\\"archive BIT_IDENTICAL           :\\\", BIT_IDENTICAL)\\nif not BIT_IDENTICAL and MEMBERS_MATCH:\\n    print(\\\"NOTE: member bytes are identical but the archive hash differs - the deflate stream differs\\\")\\n    print(\\\"      between this runtime's zlib and the packaging runtime. The verifier scores member\\\")\\n    print(\\\"      bytes, so the submission content is still reproduced; only the container differs.\\\")\\nassert MEMBERS_MATCH, \\\"payload does not reproduce the submitted member set\\\"\\nassert BIT_IDENTICAL, \\\"archive is not byte-identical to the submitted zip\\\"\"},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":\"# The competition's static packaging rules, checked on the rebuilt archive itself.\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nfails = []\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(OUT) as z:\\n    for info in z.infolist():\\n        if info.is_dir() or (info.external_attr >> 16) & 0o170000 == 0o120000:\\n            fails.append(\\\"non-regular member: %s\\\" % info.filename)\\n    names = z.namelist()\\n    top = [n for n in names if \\\"/\\\" not in n]\\n    if sorted(top) != [\\\"dqi.kmb\\\", \\\"invsqrt.kmb\\\"]:\\n        fails.append(\\\"top level members: %s\\\" % sorted(top))\\n    angles = [n for n in names if n.startswith(\\\"dfthcsos/angle_k_\\\")]\\n    if len(angles) != 15:\\n        fails.append(\\\"ANGLE circuits: %d\\\" % len(angles))\\n    if \\\"dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\" not in names:\\n        fails.append(\\\"missing dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\")\\n    npz_bytes = z.getinfo(\\\"dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\").file_size\\n    if npz_bytes > 2 ** 26:\\n        fails.append(\\\"npz too large: %d\\\" % npz_bytes)\\n    with z.open(\\\"dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\") as fh:\\n        npz = np.load(fh, allow_pickle=False)\\n        shapes = {k: npz[k].shape for k in npz.files}\\n        for k in (\\\"U\\\", \\\"W\\\", \\\"H2_I\\\", \\\"H1_I\\\", \\\"Hsym_lower\\\"):\\n            if k not in shapes:\\n                fails.append(\\\"npz missing %s\\\" % k)\\n            elif npz[k].dtype.byteorder == \\\">\\\":\\n                fails.append(\\\"npz %s is big-endian\\\" % k)\\n        if \\\"tree_edges\\\" not in shapes or not np.issubdtype(npz[\\\"tree_edges\\\"].dtype, np.integer):\\n            fails.append(\\\"npz tree_edges must be integer\\\")\\n\\nprint(\\\"npz arrays:\\\", json.dumps({k: list(v) for k, v in shapes.items()}))\\nprint(\\\"static packaging fails:\\\", fails)\\nassert not fails, fails\\nprint(\\\"STATIC_CHECKS PASS\\\")\"},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"### Result\\n\\nThe archive above is rebuilt from four public Apache-2.0 datasets with every payload file verified against the pinned SHA-256 set,\\nand it is the archive we submitted as Kaggle submission **57794709** (public **22.98999**). Member bytes and the archive hash\\n(`021ed1dd\u2026`, 28,503,982 bytes) are both hard assertions.\\n\\nNothing in this notebook evaluates, simulates or verifies a circuit \u2014 it downloads, hashes and re-packs. The three-task measurement\\nbehind the score was done separately with the official verifiers at the full shot budget; the per-task numbers are quoted in the\\nheader table so the provenance of the score is visible without re-running 200M shots here.\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}",
